\label{thm:LSD_TVA}
Suppose that Assumptions \eqref{asm:class_c}--\eqref{asm:moment_L} hold.
Then, almost surely, the ESDs of ICV and ${\mathcal A}_N$ converge to probability distributions $H$ and $F^{{\mathcal A}}$, respectively, where
\begin{equation}
H(x)=\breve{H}(x/\theta), ~~~ \textrm{for all } x\geq 0 ~ \textrm{with} ~ \theta=\int_0^1 (\gamma_t^*)^2 dt,
\label{eq: determine of H}
\end{equation}
and $F^{{\mathcal A}}$ and $H$ are related as follows:
\[
m_{{\mathcal A}}(z) = \int_{\tau\in \mathbb{R}} \frac{1}{\tilde{\theta}_f/\theta\cdot\tau(1 - \rho(1 + zm_{{\mathcal A}}(z))) - z}dH(\tau), ~~~~ \textrm{for} ~ z\in \mathbb{C}^+,
\]
where  $\tilde{\theta}_f = \int_0^1 (\dfrac 13 + \dfrac 16 f_{2,s}^*)(\gamma_s^*)^2ds$ and $m_{{\mathcal A}}(z)$ denotes the Stieltjes transform of $F^{{\mathcal A}}$.

Suppose that Assumptions \eqref{asm:class_c}-\eqref{asm:LSD_bH} and \eqref{asm:error}-\eqref{asm:interval} hold.
Then, as $p\to\infty$, the ESDs of ICV and ${\mathcal{\bm B}}_M$ converge almost surely to probability distributions $H$ and $F^{{\mathcal{\bm B}}}$, respectively, where $H$ satisfies \eqref{eq: determine of H} and $F^{{\mathcal{\bm B}}}$ is determined by $H$ in that its Stieltjes transform, $m_{{\mathcal{\bm B}}}(z)$, satisfies the Mar\v{c}enko--Pastur equation,
\begin{equation}\label{eq: m-p equation}
m_{{\mathcal{\bm B}}}(z) = \int_{\tau\in \mathbb{R}} \frac{1}{\tau(1 - c(1 + zm_{{\mathcal{\bm B}}}(z))) - z}dH(\tau),\hspace{0.2cm}\text{for}~z\in \mathbb{C^{+}}.
\end{equation}
\label{thm: theorem for the TVAPA}

